@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:product] billed-consumption-indexed-regardless-of-status
Every billed consumption unit of an agent message MUST be indexed whatever the message status,
including `created` while paused on a user question or a tool approval. A message without a
`completedAt` is indexed at its `updatedAt`.

@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:product;architecture] index-attribution-outcome-only
Indexing MUST only project the outcome of the attribution activity that ran before it: the items of
the newest attribution version, credited their stored `reconciledCreditAmountMicro`. It MUST NOT
recompute an allocation or derive credits from the message's current bill, usages or actions,
which can change between the two activities.

@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:product] consumption-items-are-billable
A consumption item MUST explain billable usage only, i.e. run usages of type `user` or
`programmatic` and the tool calls they emitted. `free` usage (a free origin such as the sidekick) is
metered but never billed, and MUST NOT produce a consumption item. Billable usage MUST be reflected
in consumption items whether or not it ends up invoiced.
